From 923bac4f8b1a6d5a12dbc676857150a8c5ce2086 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 21:24:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] meta: wait for the catalog grant to become readable before
 using it

The grant and the grant being readable are not the same event. Business asset
assignment is eventually consistent, and one function invocation on the Battle
Ground lot showed the gap:

  POST /1551227789809689/assigned_users   1.28s   succeeded
  GET  /1551227789809689/product_feeds     294ms  400, code 100 subcode 33

294ms after a successful grant the object still read as "does not exist,
cannot be loaded due to missing permissions". Pressing the same button minutes
later found it immediately and adopted it, which is the proof this is latency
rather than a wrong grant.

Losing that race is not cosmetic. The lot lands on CREATED with a dead feed,
and the only repair is a second pass that succeeds by ADOPTING the catalog the
failed run left behind -- reporting "already in your Facebook business" about a
catalog we made ninety seconds earlier, which is untrue and is the exact string
meta-master-screencast.md shot 23 says not to record.

So poll the cheapest read until it answers, 8 attempts over ~16s. Only 100/33
is treated as propagation; any other error stops immediately, because waiting
cannot fix a revoked token and burning the budget on it delays the real
message.

A timeout returns false rather than throwing. The catalog exists and the grant
is real, so the dealer is told to try again in a minute and that nothing needs
redoing on Facebook -- and the next run adopts it by name, correctly this time.

tsc --noEmit --incremental false clean; npm run build clean.

